From: Animesh Kumar <animesh.kcm@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] security: redact unseparated 9-digit SSN strings

The PII redactor currently requires a separator (dash or whitespace) between
the three digit groups of an SSN. Whisper transcripts often drop separators,
leaving sequences like "123456789" untouched. Add a second pattern that
matches a standalone 9-digit token.

This may produce false positives on long reference numbers, but for call
center transcripts a redacted reference is far better than a leaked SSN.

Reported in improvements/security-review.md#sec-02.

---
 src/security/pii_redactor.py | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/security/pii_redactor.py b/src/security/pii_redactor.py
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/src/security/pii_redactor.py
+++ b/src/security/pii_redactor.py
@@ -21,6 +21,7 @@ class PIIRedactionResult:

 PII_PATTERNS: list[tuple[str, str, str]] = [
     (r"\b\d{3}[-\s]\d{2}[-\s]\d{4}\b", "SSN", "[REDACTED_SSN]"),
+    (r"\b\d{9}\b", "SSN", "[REDACTED_SSN]"),
     (r"\b\d{4}[-\s]?\d{4}[-\s]?\d{4}[-\s]?\d{4}\b", "CREDIT_CARD", "[REDACTED_CREDIT_CARD]"),
     (r"\b[\w.+-]+@[\w-]+\.[\w.-]+\b", "EMAIL", "[REDACTED_EMAIL]"),
     (
